{"availability":"available","full":"theo-ai-lab/pacioli","name":"pacioli","description":"Did your AI actually do what it said? Pacioli checks your agent's claims against the evidence and prints a receipt you can trust. Live demo.","category":"AI & machine learning","language":"TypeScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-06-12T08:47:50Z","updated":"2026-10-09T22:00:12Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://pacioliapp.vercel.app","topics":["agent-reliability","ai-accountability","ai-agents","evals","llm-evaluation","mcp","nextjs","typescript"],"demo":"https://pacioliapp.vercel.app/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T07:01:43.637Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T07:01:43.637Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T07:01:43.637Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T07:01:43.637Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Next.js"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Double-entry bookkeeping for AI agents. Pacioli reconciles what an agent claimed it did — booked, bought, subscribed — against what the evidence shows, and prints a receipt when the two don't reconcile.","Spend trackers show you what was charged. Pacioli reconciles it against what you authorized — deterministically, with a source citation on every finding — and abstains out loud on the calls a rule cannot make.","Live demo → pacioliapp.vercel.app — paste a claim + a confirmation, get the receipt. /methods is the per-class eval · /ledger is the live record → reconcile → review loop (forward a confirmation, watch it file into your own receipt ledger) plus real, source-cited failures as receipts · or run it locally in 30 seconds (below)."],"features":["Rules before a model. The classes that are actually deterministic (a number over budget, a recurring","An LLM only on the residual, and only when measured. There are two judges behind one router: a hosted","No heavyweight backend. The riskiest assumption isn't the plumbing, it's whether a zero-setup receipt"],"sourceUr